<title>BRAZIL: CMN okays use of Brazilian Depositary Receipts.</title>
<headline>CMN okays use of Brazilian Depositary Receipts.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) has approved the creation of Brazilian Depositary Receipts, similar to their American counterparts, allowing foreign companies to trade on local bourses.</p>
<p>The BDRs, as the instruments will be known, will increase the liquidity of Brazilian stock exchanges, Francisco da Costa e Silva, the head of the Stock Exchange Commission said.</p>
<p>Several foreign companies have requested that they be allowed to trade in Brazil, Costa e Silva said.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
</text>
